Why This Is Asked

Tests cross-region DVA design with production-grade guarantees.

Key Concepts
- Exactly-once semantics via per-eventId deduplication and conditional writes
- Schema evolution using a registry and partitioned Parquet sinks
- Late-arrival handling with 24-hour backfill window and idempotent reprocessing
- Observability: CloudWatch metrics, DLQ, and alerting
- Trade-offs: cost, latency, and cross-region consistency

Code Example

```javascript
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const ddb = new AWS.DynamoDB.DocumentClient();

async function saveEvent(event) {
  const params = {
    TableName: process.env.TABLE_NAME,
    Item: {
      deviceId: event.deviceId,
      eventId: event.eventId,
      timestamp: event.timestamp,
      data: event.data
    },
    ConditionExpression: 'attribute_not_exists(eventId)'
  };

  try {
    await ddb.put(params).promise();
  } catch (error) {
    if (error.code !== 'ConditionalCheckFailedException') {
      throw error;
    }
  }
}
```

